WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:01.950
- Dwarf goblins.

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:03.420
I mean, she literally looks like a goblin.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.560
I'm just telling you,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.760
and acts like a goblin.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.490
- Just because you claim
to think something is true,

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:09.930
does not make it true.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:12.780
- The jury awards almost
50 million in damages

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.210
against Alex Jones and
his companies for defaming

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:18.030
the parents of children killed
in the Sandy Hook massacre.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.460
After years of being
targeted by Alex Jones,

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.500
the parents finally had their
chance to address Jones,

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.910
to his face, in court.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:27.210
And things did not go well for Jones.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.920
Just how bad was it?

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.327
So bad that former Prosecutor
Mitchell Epner said,

00:00:31.327 --> 00:00:33.240
"In over 25 years as a trial lawyer,

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.550
I have never seen a witness
do more damage to himself

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.020
on the stand than Alex Jones.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.150
And that includes a case where I was AUSA,

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.310
where I got a defendant to
admit that he was guilty

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.650
of the crime charged in the indictment."

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.807
It was so bad that also, former
Prosecutor Ken White said,

00:00:46.807 --> 00:00:47.650
"It was like an action movie

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:50.040
where it's not enough
that the bad guy gets shot

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.090
or stabbed at the end.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.820
He's gotta be like decapitated
and exploded and impaled

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.810
at the same time."

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.010
But let's start at the beginning.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.690
Why was Alex Jones on trial?

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.870
In 2012, a lone gunman murdered
six adults and 20 children

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.600
at the Sandy Hook Elementary
School in Newtown, Connecticut.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:04.966
Alex Jones and his
associate, Alan Shroyer,

00:01:04.966 --> 00:01:08.490
and Wolfgang Helbig said
that the event was a hoax

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:09.685
that did not happen.

00:01:09.685 --> 00:01:11.280
- The whole thing was a giant hoax.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.590
- The Jones gang accused
the bereaved family members

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.510
of being, quote, "crisis actors".

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.270
- And it just shows how bold they are,

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.640
that they clearly used actors.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.040
- And Jones and his correspondence
repeated those claims

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.480
on "Infowars" broadcast.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.620
- Okay, so just another
question that people are now

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:30.750
going to be asking about Sandy Hook.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.390
- Alex Jones' fans
harassed the parents online

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:34.223
and at their homes.

00:01:34.223 --> 00:01:35.550
And after several years of this,

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:38.040
some of the Sandy Hook families
sued Jones for defamation

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.810
in Connecticut and Texas.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.480
During his deposition in one
of the other Sandy Hook cases,

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.490
lawyers played clips of
Jones mocking the parents

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.470
and calling their tears bad acting.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:47.880
- The only problem is that I've watched

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:51.333
a lot of soap operas, and
I've seen actors before.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:53.520
And I know when I'm watching a movie

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:54.750
and I know when I'm
watching something real.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.010
- And in response to those clips,

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:56.940
Jones admitted under oath

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.650
that he knew his statements were false.

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:00.028
After his deposition Jones and "Infowars"

00:02:00.028 --> 00:02:02.244
denied having emails, text messages,

00:02:02.244 --> 00:02:04.921
and other material about
the Sandy Hook claims.

00:02:04.921 --> 00:02:07.770
Jones and his lawyers
then ignored court orders

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.080
to produce documents in
Texas and Connecticut.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.390
And spoiler alert,
during the damages trial,

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.880
we found out that they lied
about having this material

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.520
when one of his lawyers accidentally sent

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.620
Jones's entire cell phone

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.230
and a whole bunch of other
documents to opposing counsel.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:23.850
- Your attorneys messed up

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:26.910
and sent me an entire digital copy

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:30.360
of your entire cell phone
with every text message

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.700
you've sent for the past two years.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:33.780
- And Jones has a whole pattern

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.430
of disregarding discovery obligations

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.260
in other cases as well.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.750
And some people have claimed that Jones

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.360
has gotten railroaded by having liability

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.670
conceded by default.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:48.005
And that Jones's constitutional
rights have been infringed.

00:02:48.005 --> 00:02:50.730
That is not the case here.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:54.780
Here, it was a strategic choice
by Jones and his attorney

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.790
to not turn documents over,

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.590
all the while claiming
that they never possessed

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.200
relevant documents and that
those documents didn't exist.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.180
We know now that that is not the case,

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:05.970
that it was a strategic choice
to hold those documents back,

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:06.900
and never turn them over

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.690
and then face the repercussions in court,

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:11.220
which is what they basically have done,

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.990
and why liability was conceded.

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:15.660
- But I'm not going to seal the entire

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.810
quantity of information
without knowing what's in it

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:21.060
when the rules weren't followed properly.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.740
- And taking all of
that into consideration,

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.992
the judges in all 10
Sandy Hook cases entered

00:03:24.992 --> 00:03:28.260
default judgements against
Jones and his companies.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.940
A default judgment
happens when the defendant

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.335
in a civil case fails to do something,

00:03:32.335 --> 00:03:35.160
such as ignoring court
summons, missing a court date,

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:38.040
or disregarding the judges direct orders.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.230
And if this occurs, a
court may rule in favor

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.820
of the plaintiff by default.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.200
And this is very rare.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.880
A default judgment is
the most serious sanction

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.650
a judge can impose during a civil trial.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:49.200
Judges do not enter default
judgements very often.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.120
But if you want to learn more about why

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.980
the default judgements
were entered against Jones,

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.330
check out my video on the topic.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:57.570
I have an entire video
on the predamages portion

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.403
of this trial.

00:03:58.403 --> 00:03:59.940
But this particular case that
we're talking about today

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.740
is the first of three upcoming trials

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:04.350
that will decide how much
money Jones and his companies

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:05.460
must pay in damages.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:07.560
It was filed by Neil
Heslin and Scarlett Lewis,

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.720
who are the parents of
six-year-old, Jesse Lewis,

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.100
who was killed at Sandy Hook.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.900
And since the default
judgments were issued,

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.430
Jones couldn't contest liability.

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:17.700
The trial was only about
how much Jones must pay.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.620
And the plaintiff sought $150 million

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.630
in compensatory and punitive damages.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:23.880
So what did the plaintiff
say during trial?

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.610
Well, Neil Heslin was the
first plaintiff to testify.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:31.020
- I can't even describe
the last 9 1/2 years

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:36.020
of the living hell that I
and others have had to endure

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:39.418
because of the negligence
and the recklessness

00:04:39.418 --> 00:04:40.910
of Alex Jones.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:42.690
- He and Lewis said that strangers

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:45.090
have confronted them everywhere,
including at their homes.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.310
Heslin's house and car
have been shot by people

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:48.690
yelling out, "Alex Jones."

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:51.247
- But he drove by my home,
shouting out the window,

00:04:51.247 --> 00:04:55.200
"Alex Jones", and sounded like gunfire

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.910
coming from the vehicle.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:58.530
- Heslin gave heart-wrenching testimony

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:01.170
about holding his son and
seeing that he had a bullet hole

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:02.280
through his head.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:04.350
Owen Shroyer went on Jones' program

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:07.470
and said that Heslin lied about
the holding his son's body.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.030
- [Owen] I think it's time for you

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:12.000
to explain this contradiction
in the narrative.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.100
- And this is apparently what
prompted Heslin and Lewis

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:14.933
to fight back.

00:05:14.933 --> 00:05:16.143
- Alex started this fight,

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:19.590
and I'll finish this fight.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.120
- Now, Jones wasn't in court

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.250
to hear Heslin's testimony about Jesse.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:25.350
It's not necessary to show up to court,

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:27.930
but you know, usually
you do want to do that.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.120
Instead, while Heslin testified,

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.120
Jones did a live show
where he called Heslin slow

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.770
and autistic and accused him

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.480
of being manipulated by lawyers.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.340
- But I'll just say
'cause I gotta be honest,

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:40.020
he's slow, okay?

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:42.540
- This was not a good
strategy because this clip

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:46.183
was then played in court for
the jury just a few days later.

00:05:46.183 --> 00:05:48.900
- I mean, I been Heslin acts
like somebody on the spectrum.

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:50.700
- It supported one of the
plaintiff's key claims

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.920
that Jones has spent years ridiculing

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.240
the Sandy Hook parents,

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:56.345
and that he can't control
himself or his employees

00:05:56.345 --> 00:05:58.650
who continue to harass the families.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:01.590
Now after court, Heslin and
Jones had a confrontation

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.170
where Jones again called
Heslin a slow person

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:05.700
who's being manipulated by lawyers.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.520
Jones also ripped the judge
on his "Infowars" program.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:11.040
- And they're all caricatures
of what you would imagine

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:15.690
in some alternate
universe of dwarf goblins.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:17.370
It's demonic.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:20.820
They all act demonically
possessed, the judge, the lawyers.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:22.830
- Now part of our job as
lawyers is client control.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:25.650
We tell our clients not to talk
about their cases in public.

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:26.730
Don't post a Facebook.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.220
Don't share things in the media.

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:30.600
Don't talk with friends and family,

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.730
but ultimately though,
it's up to the client

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:34.530
to demonstrate some self-control.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:36.243
- Judge Goblin here in Austin,

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:38.580
I mean, she literally looks like a goblin,

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.010
I'm just telling you,
and acts like a goblin.

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:42.549
- Even the greatest lawyers in history

00:06:42.549 --> 00:06:45.510
would probably be powerless to stop Jones

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:47.580
from being himself.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:48.450
And then there was the testimony

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:49.949
of plaintiff Scarlett Lewis.

00:06:49.949 --> 00:06:52.200
Jones was again, not in
court for the first half

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.760
of Scarlett Lewis's testimony.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:54.930
When he finally arrived,

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.060
he was accompanied by
a team of bodyguards.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:59.564
Lewis addressed her
testimony directly to Jones

00:06:59.564 --> 00:07:01.560
while he sat at the defense table.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:04.350
- I am a mother first and foremost.

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:06.330
And I know that you're a father.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:08.850
And my son existed.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:10.023
I know you believe me.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:14.370
And yet, you're gonna
leave this courthouse

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:16.470
and you're gonna say
it again on your show.

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.330
- At one point Lewis directly asked Jones-

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.713
- You think I'm an actress?

00:07:22.613 --> 00:07:23.446
- [Alex] No, I don't think you're

00:07:23.446 --> 00:07:24.279
an actress.
- No,

00:07:24.279 --> 00:07:25.560
you can't talk right now.
- Sorry.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.630
- Now Lewis told Jones
that he makes claims

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.970
about the massacre that he knows are lies.

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:32.220
- But when you say those things,

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:35.133
there's a fringe of
society that believe you,

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:37.950
that are actually dangerous.

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:39.540
- And Lewis emphasized the deep trauma

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:41.820
that she has because of
Jones and his followers.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:46.820
- It seems so incredible to
me that we have to do this,

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:56.643
that we have to implore you,

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.550
not just implore you,

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:03.270
punish you to get you to stop lying.

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:04.748
- A forensic psychologist
who met Heslin and Lewis

00:08:04.748 --> 00:08:07.050
said both suffer from a form

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:08.520
of post-traumatic stress disorder

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:11.010
that comes from constant trauma.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:12.900
Jones's lawyer, Reynal, had a tough time

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:14.880
handling these witnesses
on cross examination

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:16.440
because it would be incredibly hard

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:18.300
to cross examine these witnesses.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.160
At one point, he suggested
that it would be more healing

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:21.720
for Lewis and Heslin to sit down

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.280
and talk through their
trauma with Alex Jones

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.110
than it would to file a lawsuit.

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:27.570
On cross-examination,
Jones' lawyer grilled Lewis

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:29.460
about her finances,
noting her book contract

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:30.600
and speaking engagements.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:32.850
- [Federico] Can you tell the
members of the jury how much

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:34.410
is this suggested honorarium

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.620
and for your speaking engagement?

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.083
- It may be $5,000.

00:08:41.561 --> 00:08:42.927
- [Federico] Would 10 be more accurate?

00:08:42.927 --> 00:08:43.760
- It could be 10.

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:45.450
- And he said that she makes
more than enough to pay

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:46.530
for her own therapy.

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:48.810
Now I'm gonna go out on a limb here

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:49.890
and say that this questioning

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:52.800
probably did not go over
particularly well with the jury.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.110
And then there's the testimony
of Alex Jones himself.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.270
When he took the stand, he told plaintiffs

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.100
that he's always wanted to apologize.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:02.130
- That I never intentionally
tried to hurt you.

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:06.570
I never even said your name
until this case came to court.

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.130
I didn't even really know who you were

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:10.630
until a couple years ago
when all this started up.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:12.960
The internet had a lot of questions.

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:13.950
I had questions.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:15.570
- Jones argued that he
made a few inquiries

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:18.270
about whether Sandy Hook
was a false flag operation.

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:20.490
And then the mainstream media
reported on what he said

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:22.140
and turned everything into a circus.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:25.170
The media, Jones said,
created an atmosphere

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:27.210
where nobody knew what the facts were.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.550
So there was no real way
for him to get it right.

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:31.680
Jones and his lawyer argued
that the Sandy Hook parents

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:34.110
were victimized four times,
by the shooter, by truthers,

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:37.050
by politicians, and by everyone
else who took their grief

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:38.220
and weaponized it.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.440
In other words, it wasn't his fault.

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:41.786
Now on cross-examination,
Jones also admitted

00:09:41.786 --> 00:09:44.160
that he'd basically
called every major event

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.920
of the last decade a false
flag incident engineered

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:47.753
by the government.

00:09:47.753 --> 00:09:49.830
And the judge was not
pleased by any of this.

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:51.330
You've probably seen the incendiary clips

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:54.450
of the judge telling Jones
to stop lying under oath.

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:57.033
- You're already under
oath to tell the truth.

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:02.250
You've already violated
that oath twice, today.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:03.240
- Now the judge admonished Jones

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:04.500
for a number of different things.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.960
The first was telling the
jury that he was bankrupt.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:10.500
Jones repeatedly testified that
he only makes money selling

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.130
prepackaged prepper food
for like an apocalypse.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.950
Everything else was
money-losing that he claimed,

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:19.110
but plaintiffs had already
shown that "Infowars"

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:20.550
was making a lot of money,

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:23.400
as much as $800,000 a day
during certain events.

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:25.380
And one of his employees
testified that the company

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:27.570
makes about $50 million annually.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:29.306
- That's what the documents says.

00:10:29.306 --> 00:10:31.620
- Though faced with three upcoming trials,

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:35.040
Jones and his companies have
started bankruptcy proceedings.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.363
Now when a company files
for chapter 11 protection,

00:10:37.363 --> 00:10:41.010
it tends to stay the
other legal proceedings.

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:43.920
Jones has many LLCs,
but the biggest company

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:45.510
is Free Speech Systems.

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:48.060
Free Speech Systems filed
for bankruptcy in Texas.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:51.120
So Jones's lawyer moved to stay
the Connecticut proceedings,

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:52.950
which is a different case.

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:54.990
But this was the second
delay in the Connecticut case

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:56.490
because of bankruptcy maneuvers.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:11:00.030
Back in April, "Infowars"
and two of its subsidiaries,

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:02.970
Infowars Health LLC,
and Prison Planet LLC,

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:04.890
also filed for bankruptcy protection.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:07.620
Now these entities were
removed as named defendants

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:10.020
so that the damages
proceeding could move forward.

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:13.290
Now Free Speech Systems
listed 14.3 million in assets,

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:15.330
including over a million dollars in cash,

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:17.760
and almost 1.6 million in
property and equipment.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:20.790
However, the petition claimed
the company had 79 million

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:24.450
in liabilities, including
a $54 million debt owed

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.060
to something called PQPR Holdings.

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:29.100
Now who owns PQPR Holdings?

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:31.200
Well it's Carol Jones and David Jones,

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:33.810
also known as Alex Jones' mom and dad.

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:34.770
Now the Sandy Hook plaintiffs

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:37.410
believe the bankruptcy
proceedings are a sham.

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:40.333
Heslin, Pozner, and two
other Sandy Hook families

00:11:40.333 --> 00:11:42.900
filed separate lawsuits, accusing Jones

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:45.000
of hiding millions of dollars in assets.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.670
The plaintiff said the $54
million debt was dubious

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:48.503
since PQPR is a Nevada-registered company

00:11:48.503 --> 00:11:51.480
that is owned by shell entities

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.821
owned by Jones' kids and parents.

00:11:53.821 --> 00:11:56.850
There's substantial evidence
of fraudulent transfers.

00:11:56.850 --> 00:11:58.260
And it's not even clear
that the bankruptcy court

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:00.600
would discharge the Sandy
Hook judgments anyway.

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:04.560
So while Jones may delay, it's
likely to be a pure victory.

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:06.300
And going back to what
Jones was admonished

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:07.470
for during the trial,

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:09.090
Jones told the jury that he had complied

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:10.290
with the court's discovery orders,

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:12.360
which is absolutely false.

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:13.241
Now, during discovery,
plaintiffs asked for a number

00:12:13.241 --> 00:12:14.730
of different things,

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:17.190
but they specifically asked
Jones to identify the number

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:18.990
of videos he produced about Sandy Hook.

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:20.880
Jones and his co-defendants
refused to produce

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:22.560
this material, which is one of the reasons

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:23.640
for the default judgment.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:24.660
And the plaintiff's lawyer has generally

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:26.648
had a pretty easy time
showing that Alex Jones

00:12:26.648 --> 00:12:29.580
was lying about the stuff
that was actually produced.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:30.587
- Mr. Reynal had told the jury

00:12:30.587 --> 00:12:34.013
that there was 29 minutes
total of "Infowars" videos.

00:12:34.013 --> 00:12:36.990
He played 51 minutes in a single video.

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:38.430
So, you know that's not true.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:42.540
He has routinely, every
single day of this trial,

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:45.540
broken rules that a
first-year lawyer knows.

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:48.720
He has routinely placed
inadmissible material

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:49.800
in front of the jury.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.360
It is from our perspective of this table

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:54.540
that Mr. Reynal is actively
trying for mistrial.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.280
- And the judge told Alex Jones's lawyer

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:57.960
to stop many different times.

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:02.960
- I am very upset that you
have tried to imply to the jury

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:09.080
that we know how many videos
about Sandy Hook were released

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:12.000
by your clients when we don't

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:15.450
because they refused to
respond to discovery.

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:18.060
So I do not want you to do that again.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.880
And I don't want you to
argue with me about it.

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:23.190
That is the rule of this case.

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:26.310
That's it, they didn't respond.

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:27.720
We don't know.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:30.780
We've had multiple
conversations about how I know

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:31.980
you know what the rules are,

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:34.260
and you know you know what the rules are,

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:36.990
but you've chosen not to
follow them on occasion.

00:13:36.990 --> 00:13:38.580
- And despite the judge's
very clear instructions

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:39.690
on the number of videos,

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:41.458
Reynal interrupted the judge to argue.

00:13:41.458 --> 00:13:45.540
- The number of videos, their length,

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:47.433
this is evidence that is being
introduced in the courtroom.

00:13:47.433 --> 00:13:50.257
- Yes, but what you said was not,

00:13:50.257 --> 00:13:53.400
"We've shown the jury 29 minutes of clips

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:56.130
where the word Sandy Hook
appears," or anything like that.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:14:00.720
It was, "They released
in total 29 minutes."

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:01.920
That is not true.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:04.291
- The judge made it
extraordinarily clear to Alex Jones

00:14:04.291 --> 00:14:06.060
what he could and could not do.

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:08.740
- You may not say to this jury

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:12.333
that you complied with discovery.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:15.540
That is not true.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.163
You may not say it again.

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:22.470
You may not tell this jury
that you are bankrupt.

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:25.140
That is also not true.

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:27.753
You're already under
oath to tell the truth.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:33.300
You've already violated
that oath twice, today,

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:35.730
in just those two examples.

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:40.730
It seems absurd to instruct you again,

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:44.340
that you must tell the
truth while you testify,

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:45.570
yet, here I am.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:48.810
You must tell the truth while you testify.

00:14:48.810 --> 00:14:51.183
This is not your show.

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:55.690
You need to slow down

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:00.630
and not take what you see as opportunities

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:05.630
to further the message you
are wanting to further.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:11.630
And instead, only answer the
specific and exact question

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:13.770
you have been asked.

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:15.390
- Now, what makes all of these exchanges

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:19.320
particularly remarkable is
that Jones's lawyer Reynal

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:21.750
probably knew that there
was a ticking time bomb

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:25.080
that disproved Jones's
claims about discovery.

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:26.970
The ticking time bomb
was that Jones's lawyer

00:15:26.970 --> 00:15:28.637
had accidentally sent 300 gigabytes

00:15:28.637 --> 00:15:31.770
of unredacted information
directly to plaintiff's counsel.

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:35.610
And that included Jones's
entire cell phone backup.

00:15:35.610 --> 00:15:37.350
And sure enough, on cross examination,

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:39.660
a plaintiff's lawyer,
Bankston reminded Jones

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:42.450
that he claimed to have
searched for messages related

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:44.310
to Sandy Hook on his phone.

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:47.490
Jones said yes, that he did
the search, but found nothing.

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:49.272
- So you did get my text messages

00:15:49.272 --> 00:15:51.028
and said you didn't?

00:15:51.028 --> 00:15:51.861
Nice trick.

00:15:51.861 --> 00:15:54.390
- And that led to the Perry
Mason moment where Bankston

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:57.120
absolutely skewered Jones
on cross examination

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:59.700
by pointing out that
these documents did exist

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:01.500
in the form of text messages and emails

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:03.150
that mentioned Sandy Hook.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:06.180
And the reason that Bankston
knew that they existed

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:08.280
is because Jones's lawyer
accidentally sent him

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:09.690
the entire cell phone.

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:11.103
- I see, I told you the truth.

00:16:11.103 --> 00:16:13.050
This is your Perry Mason moment.

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:16.440
- Yeah, that's quite the exchange.

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:18.720
And in fact, I have an
entire video covering

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:20.910
both this Perry Mason moment,

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:23.520
and the equally interesting hearing

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:24.420
that was held the next day

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:27.000
where the defense council
moved for mistrial.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:30.360
And that also did not
go well for Alex Jones.

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:32.280
But since liability was already conceded,

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:35.130
it didn't really take the jury
very long to award damages

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:36.180
to the plaintiffs.

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:39.300
The jury found that Alex
Jones should pay $4.1 million

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:41.850
in compensatory damages
for repeatedly claiming

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.267
the school shooting was a hoax.

00:16:43.267 --> 00:16:45.600
Now a court awards compensatory damages

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:47.040
to put the plaintiff in the situation

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:49.710
that they would've been,
had the harm not occurred.

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:51.810
Now compensatory damages
include both economic

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:54.570
and noneconomic damages, such
as medical bills, lost wages,

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.310
pain and suffering, mental impairment,

00:16:56.310 --> 00:16:57.360
and emotional distress.

00:16:57.360 --> 00:17:00.780
Heslin and Lewis were seeking
$150 million from Jones,

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:03.840
but the jury's verdict fell
pretty far short of that mark.

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:08.078
Jones's lawyer, Reynal, asked
jurors to award a total of $8.

00:17:08.078 --> 00:17:11.310
$1 for each of the eight
harms the defendants inflicted

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:12.900
on Heslin and Lewis.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:14.310
Of course, he couldn't ask for nothing

00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:16.140
because liability was conceded.

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:18.360
Now the jury's verdict was not unanimous.

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:20.130
Two of the juries did not sign the form.

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:24.510
In Texas, civil jury verdict
does not have to be unanimous.

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:26.520
But that takes us to the punitive damages,

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:28.830
or as Texas calls them, exemplary damages.

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:31.980
Now, a court will award
exemplary damages in Texas

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:35.850
to punish the wrongdoer for
their particularly bad behavior.

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:38.730
Exemplary damages are
also meant to deter people

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:41.340
who might act like the
defendant in the future.

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:43.590
So in other words, Texas exemplary damages

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:46.191
are meant to penalize the
defendant for their behavior

00:17:46.191 --> 00:17:48.570
and to warn others not
to do the same thing.

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:51.840
And under section 41.003,

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:54.318
the Texas Code of Practice and Remedies,

00:17:54.318 --> 00:17:57.390
exemplary damages are
awarded to a plaintiff

00:17:57.390 --> 00:17:59.550
if they prove with clear
and convincing evidence

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:01.800
that they're harm resulted
from fraud, malice,

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.330
or gross negligence.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:05.760
But exemplary damages may only be awarded

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:07.950
if the decision is unanimous.

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:09.810
This, in combination with the
clear and convincing evidence

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:12.330
standard makes it difficult
to recover exemplary damages

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:14.190
in personal injury cases in Texas.

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:15.990
But there's another
wrinkle because in Texas,

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:18.180
there's a statutory
cap on punitive damages

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:19.557
in personal injury cases.

00:18:19.557 --> 00:18:24.000
An award of exemplary damages
may not exceed an amount equal

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:27.089
to the greater of two
times the economic damages

00:18:27.089 --> 00:18:30.450
plus an amount equal to
any non-economic damages

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:35.450
found by the jury, not to
exceed $750,000 or $200,000.

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.640
And another subsection
prohibits telling the jury

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:40.260
about this particular cap.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:42.900
Now, the reason the
juries are not instructed

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:45.180
is that that might
influence their thinking.

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:46.680
They might shift punitive damages

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.750
into the compensatory damages.

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:50.760
So it's entirely possible
that the jury can come up

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:53.303
with a much bigger amount
than the statute allows.

00:18:53.303 --> 00:18:55.740
And if a jury returns
an award that is higher

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:56.940
than the statutory cap,

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:59.250
then the judge just
simply reduces the amount.

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:01.590
And in closing arguments, the
plaintiffs attorney argued

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:04.297
that this was the jury's ability
to send a message to quote,

00:19:04.297 --> 00:19:06.480
"Stop Alex Jones, stop the monetization

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:08.160
of misinformation of lies."

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:11.520
The defense argued that
Jones had only spent 18 hours

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:13.290
and 43 minutes talking about Sandy Hook,

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:16.350
and that they only made
about $14,000 per hour

00:19:16.350 --> 00:19:17.183
during the coverage.

00:19:17.183 --> 00:19:20.430
And that should form
the basis of the award.

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:21.840
And following closing arguments,

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.600
the jury returned to
verdict of $45 million

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:25.740
in punitive damages.

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:28.020
But given the statutory limits
that we just talked about,

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:30.000
it's likely that the
punitive damages award

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.550
is likely to get chopped down to well less

00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:33.900
than a million dollars.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:36.510
But that raises the question
what's next for Alex Jones?

00:19:36.510 --> 00:19:38.220
Well, the answer is more trials.

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:41.490
On September 14th, the Pozner
and De La Rosa plaintiffs

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.784
will face Jones in Texas courtroom.

00:19:43.784 --> 00:19:47.610
In addition, Jones may find
himself in deeper trouble

00:19:47.610 --> 00:19:49.050
with the January 6th Committee,

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:51.510
